# Push verification (before `git push origin main`)

When the user asks to **push**, **ship**, or you finish web changes intended for `main`:

Run checks first. Push with `git push origin main` (or the branch they named) — do **not** use a wrapper that auto-commits.

**Commit gate first:** product commits must already have passed scoped production build per always-on [`lint-build-before-commit.mdc`](./lint-build-before-commit.mdc). Do not invent a commit that skipped that gate. Next build already runs ESLint — do not add a separate `npm run lint` hard step for the same workspace.

## Required order (do not skip or reorder)

1. `npm run build` when changes touch `apps/web/**` product inputs (app/lib/types/components/env/build config); `npm run build:ops` when changes touch `apps/ops/**` or `packages/shared/**` (sequential if both)
2. Targeted unit tests for touched logic, e.g. `node --import tsx --test apps/web/src/lib/<name>.test.ts`
3. `git push origin main` (after local commit / merge as the user asked)

If the tree is unchanged since a documented build pass from the commit gate, step 1 may be treated as already satisfied; any edit after that pass → re-run build.

## Prohibited

- Push without `npm run build` when web product inputs changed (or without `build:ops` when ops/shared changed)
- Use `npx tsx --test` (use `node --import tsx --test` instead)
- Run build/test **in parallel** with each other
- Require a separate full-project `npm run lint` when the scoped Next build already passed (build embeds ESLint)
- Use Multitask / background subagents for small tasks (roughly ≤5 files, single feature)

## Efficiency

- One linear pipeline: build → test → push
- Do not open Multitask for cleanup-only or push-only follow-ups unless the user explicitly requests it
